KEPT FORM (commit ab813be2e). In get_cam_wpos's `if (gNumTransmitters == 0 && lbl_803443F8 <= 0)` block, AFTER the `for (i=0;i<4;i++) camState[i]=0;` loop, an inner brace block opens with exactly:
        {
        f32 lat = lbl_80345EC8;
        f64 yawMax = lbl_80345F58;
        f64 yawMin = lbl_80345F68;
        f64 yawRange = lbl_80345F60;
        f64 yawStep = lbl_80346180;
and the loop body's `place_cam(cam, mat, in, out);` is replaced by place_cam's body written out with `lat` substituted for the two lbl_80345EC8 reads:
            CreateYPRMatrix(mat, cam->pyr);
            in[0] = lat;
            in[1] = lat;
            in[2] = cam->radius;
            WorldVector(in, &out[6], mat);
            cam->wpos[0] = cam->attn[0] + out[6];
            cam->wpos[1] = cam->attn[1] + out[7];
            cam->wpos[2] = cam->attn[2] + out[8];
The yaw comparison uses the TU's own byte-verified sibling spelling (combat.c:310-313/724-727): `if (y > yawMax) { y = y - yawRange; } else if (y <= yawMin) { y = yawRange + y; }` -- note `y = y - yawRange`, NOT `y -= yawRange`. The other five place_cam call sites are left CALLING place_cam unchanged; that is load-bearing (see axis_log D).
